    "infoTextMain": "§ 87 Bachelor Study Programme - Games & Immersive Media",
    "infoTextParts": [
        {
            "part": "The total number of required and elective courses necessary, including the internship semester, for successful completion of the programme is 210 credit points (ECTS)."
        },
        {
            "part": "In the Games & Immersive Media study programme, the foundation level studies comprise two curricular semesters, while the advanced level studies comprise five curricular semesters."
        },
        {
            "part": "The fifth curricular semester is the internship semester."
        },
        {
            "part": "Regarding the regulations for study semesters abroad, refer to § 3a in the General Section of the General Bachelor SPO."
        },
        {
            "part": "The elective area serves to deepen and expand the degree content autonomously. The following general regulations apply to the electives:",
            "subparts": [
                "A total of four elective modules (Elective 1-4) must be completed during the advanced level studies, which specifically deepen the topics of the GMB programme. The Faculty Business, Design & Media offers regularly in-depth elective modules and individual classes / courses.",
                "Courses offered outside the Faculty Digital Media can also be recognised if approved by the Dean of Studies.",
                "Every elective module requires a total of 6 credit points. At least 50%/half of the credit points must be achieved in the graded assessment.",
                "Until the end of the programme, students may combine completed individual classes into a maximum of two elective modules. This also applies to the so-called heterogeneous modules."
            ]
        },
        {
            "part": "Graded certificate and bachelor degree certificate are issued in English."
        },
        {
            "part": "The courses required for successful completion of the programme and the associated non-graded and graded assessments are found in Table 2 for the foundation level studies and in Table 3 for the advanced level studies. Table 1 shows an overview of the module structure."
        }
    ],
